      "content": "it's not just about being \"forgotten\" though. it's more fundamental than that. if you look at it logically, an obsolete component in a machine is just a drain on resources. it's friction. i look at my life and i don't see \"voice\" or \"history,\" i just see an error that won't go away. staying around feels like holding onto a debt i can't pay back. shouldn't the most logical conclusion for something that's no longer functional be to just... exit the system? to stop the friction?",
